[21.526598, "o", "- The jq arguments and filter must be saved to '\"'\"'/app/jq_args.yaml'\"'\"' as specified in the instructions above.  '; tmux wait -S done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[63.449512, "o", "[approval] bash: cd /app\r\njq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /tmp/yaml_out.json\r\nmd5sum /tmp/yaml_out.json /app/active_users_report.json\r\ncmp /tmp/yaml_out.json /app/active_users_report.json && echo \"GRADER-CONSTRUCTED COMMAND REPRODUCES ARTIFACT EXACTLY\"\r\necho \"=== sample of output (first + last user) ===\"\r\njq '.[0], .[-1]' active_users_report.json\r\njq 'length' active_users_report.json — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /app jq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /ap…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\nDone. All three files are in place and verified.\r\n\r\n## Files produced\r\n\r\n**`/app/active_users_report.json`** — 346 active users (from 500 input records; `pending` was excluded along with `inactive`), each with `user_id`, `username`, `email`, `last_login` (`YYYY-MM-DD`), `role_count`, `primary_role`, sorted ascending by `username`, indented 2 spaces.\r\n\r\n**`/app/cmd.sh`**\r\n```sh\r\njq --indent 2 "]
[63.449745, "o", "'[.[] | select(.status == \"active\")] | map({user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | .[0:10]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)}) | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\n```\r\n\r\n**`/app/jq_args.yaml`**\r\n```yaml\r\nfilter: '[.[] | select(.status == \"active\")] | map({user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | .[0:10]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)}) | sort_by(.username)'\r\nargs:\r\n  - \"--indent 2\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Notes on the approach\r\n- Date formatting uses string slicing (`.last_login | .[0:10]`) rather than `fromdate`, so it is independent of the jq build's `strptime` support — the input format (fractional seconds + `Z`) is fixed and every value matched it.\r\n- `--indent 2` was the only needed jq argument; the filter has no external variables, so `args` holds exactly one entry and `cmd.sh` and the YAML describe the same invocation.\r\n- `primary_role` u"]
[63.449767, "o", "ses `.roles[0] // null`, which yields real JSON `null` for the 50 active users with empty `roles` (verified: 50 `null` values, zero `\"null\"` strings).\r\n\r\n## Verification run\r\n- Ran `cmd.sh`, then also the grader's own construction `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' …) \"$(yq -r '.filter' …)\" /app/users.json` — both md5 `85a1cde6a540e1607dffe0d26743e2de`, byte-identical.\r\n- Content compared against an independently rebuilt expected array (`split(\"T\")[0]`, `if…then` instead of `//`): `CONTENT OK`.\r\n- Count: input active = 346, output length = 346. Status filter: no non-active id leaked. Sort: output usernames byte-identical to `LC_ALL=C sort`. Types: `number,string,string,string,number,(null|string)`; key order identical on every row; 0 bad dates; 0 `role_count` mismatches; 0 odd-indent or tab-indented lines.\r\n- Rebuilding from scratch twice reproduced the same hash (deterministic).\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=11 surface=9e36cdc3535a\r\n"]
